    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118-a1">

                <pb facs="0415" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg313"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt’s Adviser</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baruch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-17">May 17 (?), 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum on Magnesium</hi>:</p>
                <p>Unless there are demands for lend-lease and for our Armed Forces, which were not
                    ordered up to the <hi rendition="#italic">afternoon of May 17, 1943</hi>, supply
                    has overtaken demand.</p>
                <p>All bins have been filled. Two months advanced shipment have been made to China
                    and Russia.</p>
                <p>A stock pile is now accumulating here at the rate of 7,500,000 lbs. per
                    month.</p>
                <p>All listed demands up to Dec. 31, 1943, will be met by production and a stock
                    pile of 50,000,000 will be accumulated by Dec. 31, 1943.</p>
                <p>There need be no anxiety over this metal unless much larger demands are
                    contemplated than have been placed. If—there are any such future requirements,
                    it should be immediately presented to the Magnesium unit of the W.P.B.
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>B. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baruch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
